format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: radioactivity

objective u2-spontaneous
statement: Know that an unstable nucleus changes by itself: nobody has to trigger it.
misconception: Decay can be switched on and off, or a person has to make an atom decay.

item u2-l1-choice-why
type: choice
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-decay

prompt:
    Why can a radioactive nucleus change even when nobody does anything to it?

options:
    {"id":"unstable","label":"It is unstable, so it can change on its own"}
    {"id":"trigger","label":"Someone must trigger it","note":"Nobody has to trigger it. Unstable nuclei change by themselves."}
    {"id":"heat","label":"It needs heat first","note":"Heating and cooling hardly affect radioactive decay."}
    {"id":"used","label":"It is being used up","note":"Nothing is used up. The nucleus changes into another nucleus."}

answer: unstable

explanation:
    An unstable nucleus can change on its own. That is what radioactive means.

