targets:
    {"id":"c12","label":"Carbon-12 nucleus","x":20,"y":24,"r":13}
    {"id":"c14","label":"Carbon-14 nucleus","x":50,"y":24,"r":13}
    {"id":"o16","label":"Oxygen-16 nucleus","x":80,"y":24,"r":13}

answer: c14
animate_on_correct: true

explanation:
    Carbon-14 is unstable, so it can change by itself. Carbon-12 and oxygen-16 are stable and stay as they are.

item u2-l1-predict-alone
type: predict
surfaces: lesson

prompt:
    An unstable nucleus is left alone for a very long time. What happens?

input: choice

options:
    {"id":"same","label":"It stays the same for ever"}
    {"id":"itself","label":"It can change by itself"}
    {"id":"trigger","label":"Someone has to trigger it"}
    {"id":"gone","label":"It disappears at once"}

answer: itself

explanation:
    Your guess is not scored. The answer comes later in the lesson.

item u2-l1-tom-person
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-decay

statement:
    A radioactive atom needs a person to make it decay.

answer: myth

explanation:
    Myth. Nobody has to make an unstable nucleus change. It changes by itself.

item u2-x-rock-alone
type: choice
difficulty: 2
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-decay

prompt:
    A rock contains unstable nuclei. Nobody touches it. What happens to those nuclei?

options:
    {"id":"some","label":"Some change on their own, now and then"}
    {"id":"wait","label":"Nothing: they wait for someone to trigger them","note":"Unstable nuclei do not need a trigger."}
    {"id":"all","label":"They all change at the same moment","note":"Each nucleus changes at its own random moment."}

answer: some

explanation:
    Unstable nuclei change by themselves. Some change now and then, and nobody can say which one is next.

item u2-x-tom-by-itself
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-decay

statement:
    An unstable nucleus changes by itself, without anyone starting it.

answer: true

explanation:
    True. Radioactive decay is spontaneous: nobody has to trigger it.
